@startuml beta-access-control
title Beta Access Control Feature Flow

' Purpose: Show the user-visible invite-only beta journey. Technical persistence and admin policy details live in architecture diagrams.

actor Visitor
actor "Invited Beta Tester" as BetaTester
actor "Non-invited User" as NonInvited
participant "Beta URL" as BetaUrl
participant "Sign-in Page" as SignIn
participant "Auth Magic-Link Email" as MagicLink
participant "Whole-App Beta Gate" as Gate
participant "Main Mushroom Mood App" as MainApp
participant "Denied / Forbidden State" as Denied

Visitor -> BetaUrl: Open deployed beta URL
BetaUrl -> Gate: Request protected page or app API

alt No valid session
  Gate --> SignIn: Show sign-in requirement
  Visitor -> SignIn: Enter email
  SignIn -> MagicLink: Send magic-link email
  Visitor -> MagicLink: Open callback link
  MagicLink --> Gate: Return signed-in email identity
else Valid session exists
  Gate -> Gate: Read signed-in email identity
end

Gate -> Gate: Normalize email and check beta allowlist

alt Signed-in email is invited
  Gate --> MainApp: Show beta app
  BetaTester -> MainApp: Run readiness flow
  MainApp --> BetaTester: Show result and explanation
else Signed-in email is not invited
  Gate --> Denied: Show invite-only denied copy
  NonInvited -> Denied: Cannot continue into beta app
else Session is invalid or expired
  Gate --> SignIn: Ask user to sign in again
end

BetaTester -> MainApp: Log out
MainApp -> Gate: Clear signed-in state
Gate --> SignIn: Return to signed-out state

note right of Gate
This feature-flow stays user-visible.
Auth.js, Resend, Drizzle, Postgres,
admin policy, feedback persistence foundation,
and other technical details live
in target architecture diagrams.
end note

@enduml
